e covered and the  fact that they think buggy got mihawk  and crocodile to yield to his authority  buggy got a bounty of  3.189 billion higher than luffy's but  interestingly enough not higher than  mihawks this is like if zoro's bounty  was higher than luffy's man this chapter  is such a flex for mihawk i gotta say  and i'm loving it and although it didn't  show buggy in the best light we can't  deny buggy's superpower of being lucky  and being able to weasel himself out of  practically every situation i do love to  hear though that the world government  considers buggy an extremely dangerous  individual even as bounties have now  clearly ceased to be an accurate gauge  of a character's actual power not saying  they were especially accurate before but  it's clearer than ever that they are not  now especially after luffy and zoro got  so lowballed now i love mihawk here he's  the one that eventually decides that  it's not that bad having buggy as a  figurehead he has no interest in the  title of emperor he just longs for peace  and what mihawk wants crocodile seems to  go with mihawk decides to let buggy have  the target on his back and adds that  they can dispose of him if the need  arises crocodile says it's true and then  we see buggy acting as leader and saying  they formed cross guild to prepare for  the new age he then introduces the new  executives crocodile and mihawk buggy is  crying because he's so unsure of what  will happen to him while his men assume  he's moved to tears because he's so  happy or something and they say they are  moved to tears as well we then catch up  with the revolutionaries as if this  chapter wasn't already hype enough most  people like me believe in sabo however  dragon says he's glad sabo is okay but  if he truly murdered king cobra then he  won't forgive him no matter what his  reasons this is definitely building the  mystery and a possible rift between  dragon and sabo who's become arguably  more famous as of late in the world of  one piece it's nice to see kuma freed in  a panel but it is sad hearing him just  talk like a slave saying i'm yours to  command master even koala tears up while  witnessing the scene we then jump to the  marines who are picking up a call that  is in fact sabo the flame emperor  calling the revolutionaries the manga  asks us will we find out the truth and  we're told we have a break next week but  wow what an amazing chapter to go on  break with this was amazing 10 out of 10  in my view even if i am a bit salty  about luffy and zoro's bounties not  being higher still the mihawk  awesomeness was so good this chapter it  arguably made up for it let me know your  thoughts on the chapter and how you  would rate it channel the parking within  and smash that like button if you  enjoyed this review and want to keep  them coming be a smashing pirate king  rather than passing orochi and youtube  will reward you with wano fireworks make  this the video you subscribe if you  haven't already and hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications or you will miss future  one-piece videos and updates and while  you wait for the next one-piece video  and chapter to drop feel free to check  out my giant and growing one-piece  playlist that includes videos in all the  yonko admirals warlords mythical zone  users and much more link to that is in  the description and on screen right now  and until next time see you space  cowboys
 

